 Why the raw line count is misleading

 GitHub reports 3,160,159 raw changed lines across his 69 PRs. Most are dependencies, not coursework code.

 For example, the ActiveRecord practice PR adds 2,951,551 lines because it includes vendored Ruby gems. After exclusions, its diff is +183 / −43.

 Three React Hooks PRs also share the exact same base and head commits. They count as three PRs, but their shared diff counts once.

 The adjusted 19,191 figure measures cumulative PR changes—not unique code, manually typed code, or productivity. Related submissions can still contain overlapping work.

 Coverage limits

 82 repositories does not mean 82 completed projects. The inventory contains starter copies, duplicate submissions, team exercises, and empty repositories.

